{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1660","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F1. Promising String (easy version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is the easy version of Problem F. The only difference between the easy version and the hard version is the constraints."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We will call a non-empty string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"balanced"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it contains the same number of plus and minus signs. For example: strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"++-+-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" are balanced, and strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \"\" are not balanced."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We will call a string "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"promising"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if the string can be made balanced by several (possibly zero) uses of the following operation:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" replace two "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"adjacent"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" minus signs with one plus sign. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In particular, every balanced string is promising. However, the converse is not true: not every promising string is balanced."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, the string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-+-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" is promising, because you can replace two adjacent minuses with plus and get a balanced string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-++-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", or get another balanced string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-+-+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"How many non-empty substrings of the given string $$$s$$$ are promising? Each non-empty promising substring must be counted in the answer as many times as it occurs in string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recall that a substring is a sequence of consecutive characters of the string. For example, for string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+-+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" its substring are: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+-+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (the string is a substring of itself) and some others. But the following strings are not its substring: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"++"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 500$$$) —the number of test cases in the test."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then the descriptions of test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case of input data consists of two lines. The first line consists of the number $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 3000$$$): the length of $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of the test case contains the string $$$s$$$ of length $$$n$$$, consisting only of characters \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of values $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$3000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print a single number: the number of the promising non-empty substrings of string $$$s$$$. Each non-empty promising substring must be counted in the answer as many times as it occurs in string $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n3\n+-+\n5\n-+---\n4\n----\n7\n--+---+\n6\n+++---\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n4\n2\n7\n4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following are the promising substrings for the first three test cases in the example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s[1 \\dots 2]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", $$$s[2 \\dots 3]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s[1 \\dots 2]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", $$$s[2 \\dots 3]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", $$$s[1 \\dots 5]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"+"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", $$$s[3 \\dots 5]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s[1 \\dots 3]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", $$$s[2 \\dots 4]$$$=\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"-"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F1","problemCode":"1660F1","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1660/problem/F1"}